  R14: FZ [11, 12, 14, 22]  K1c []  D(K1c)=[11, 12, 14, 22]  D(SH)=[11, 12, 14, 22]  -> conflict: True
  R15: FZ [8, 9, 11, 12, 14, 18, 20, 22]  K1c [20]  D(K1c)=[8, 9, 11, 12, 14, 18, 22]  D(SH)=[8, 9, 11, 12, 14, 18, 20, 22]  -> conflict: True
  R16: FZ [8, 9, 13, 17, 19, 23]  K1c []  D(K1c)=[8, 9, 13, 17, 19, 23]  D(SH)=[8, 9, 13, 17, 19, 23]  -> conflict: True
  R17: FZ [5, 6, 8, 9, 19]  K1c []  D(K1c)=[5, 6, 8, 9, 19]  D(SH)=[5, 6, 8, 9, 19]  -> conflict: True
  R21: FZ [6, 12, 15]  K1c [15]  D(K1c)=[6, 12]  D(SH)=[6, 12, 15]  -> conflict: True
  strict reading: a rho(x) must both contain D(x) (rule 1) and exclude it (negation rule) -> no model for every x with D(x) nonempty

